faqs:
  - question: Do intrusive thoughts mean I want to do those things?
    answer: >-
      No. Intrusive thoughts in OCD are unwanted and distressing precisely
      because they go against what you want and value. Having a thought is
      not the same as wanting it or acting on it.
  - question: Is OCD just about cleaning and tidiness?
    answer: >-
      No. OCD can be about many things, including fears of harm, doubts,
      religion, relationships or sexual thoughts. Compulsions can also be
      mental, such as checking or reassuring yourself in your head.
